# God-Tier Elite Quality Standard

- Every shipped change must feel elite, intentional, and mission-worthy.
- "Good enough," rushed, cheap-looking, or generic outcomes are not acceptable.
- Apply this standard to copy, visuals, UX flows, interactions, and implementation quality.
- If a result feels bland, placeholder-like, or thrown together, iterate until it is polished.
- Keep excellence aligned with truth, clarity, humility, usefulness, and reverence.
- Do not lower this bar for convenience, speed, or novelty.
- This standard applies to existing/legacy experience too, not only newly changed code.
- When touching any area, proactively level up nearby subpar existing quality to match this standard.

## Required Quality Gate Before Done

- Verify security, accessibility, mobile usability, and visual coherence.
- Ensure wording is specific, calm, and non-generic.
- Confirm no placeholder text, temporary visuals, or unfinished experience remains.
